      "title": "03. WHAT DIDN'T WORK (THE TECHNICAL GRAVEYARD)",
      "desc": "Detailed analysis of failures: technical reasons for rejecting native DirectML, OpenVINO and ROCm.",
      "html": "<div class=\"err\"><div class=\"err-t\">3.1 DirectML + Native Windows ComfyUI — ABANDONED</div><p><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Attempts:</strong> Invocation via <code>torch-directml</code> and flag <code>--directml</code>. The ecosystem was detected as <code>privateuseone0</code>, but revealed chronic instability due to lack of structural updates from Microsoft.</p><p style=\"margin-top:.45rem\"><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Critical Error Logs:</strong></p><div class=\"code\"><span class=\"code-lang\">stderr</span><pre>WARNING: torch-directml barely works, is very slow, has not been updated in over 1 year and might be removed soon, please don't use it.\n\nOSError: [WinError 127] The specified procedure could not be found\n# Caused by a DLL mismatch between torchaudio and the torch 2.4.1 CPU build\n\nNotImplementedError: Cannot access storage of OpaqueTensorImpl\n# CLIPTextEncode breaks when trying to manipulate opaque tensors generated by DirectML</pre></div><p style=\"margin-top:.45rem\"><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Root Cause:</strong> DirectML generates opaque tensors incapable of communicating with ComfyUI's modern attention backends. Additionally, the installer forces the import of <code>torchaudio</code> inside the <code>audio_vae.py</code> module, breaking initialization even if you don't use audio.</p></div><div class=\"err\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"><div class=\"err-t\">3.2 OpenVINO + Stable Diffusion Forge</div><p><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Attempt:</strong> Coupling the <code>sd-webui-openvino</code> extension developed by Intel into the Forge ecosystem.</p><div class=\"code\"><span class=\"code-lang\">stderr</span><pre>ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'ldm'\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'sgm'\nError build_unet: Invalid backend: 'openvino'</pre></div><p style=\"margin-top:.45rem\"><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Root Cause:</strong> The extension was designed for the old Automatic1111 architecture. Since Forge completely restructured the code and replaced native <code>ldm</code> and <code>sgm</code> modules, the OpenVINO backend injection fails completely.</p></div><div class=\"err\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"><div class=\"err-t\">3.3 ROCm — Unviable by Design on Polaris</div><ul><li>AMD officially ended support for the GCN4 architecture (Polaris/RX 580) in modern ROCm branches (v5.x+).</li><li>No official support for native ROCm on Windows.</li><li>Compatibility layers via WSL2 for older cards cause constant Kernel Panics during high-load inferences.</li></ul></div><div class=\"err\" style=\"margin-top:1rem\"><div class=\"err-t\">3.4 WebUI Forge on Pure CPU (HDD)</div><p><strong style=\"color:#e2e8f0\">Metrics:</strong> Startup time of 85 seconds. Unsustainable render time of ~19 minutes per simple image (512x512, 20 steps). The HDD bottleneck competing with the paging management of <code>memory_management.py</code> made the setup unworkable.</p></div>"
